mistakes you made for DNA extraction, just so you don't do them again :) 09/07/2026
- didn't add the lysis buffer to the dry sample. the fastprep is the break apart step, so if you don't do a wet sample, where you put the buffer in at the same time as the sample, you break apart the dry sample in the fastprep then you put in the lysis buffer.
- if something doesn't make sense, double check the protocol and then double check with hugo. you did a lot of unnecessary labelling. 
- you didn't turn off the certifuge (4º one) after using it. 
- you paused/ turned off the 55º degree plate but didn't check when you turned it back on that it was at 55º. 

